package server

const mcpFlowchartPolicy = "IBM Flowcharting is the ibm-flowcharting template on existing type:flowchart, with optional node.flowchartSymbol using stable ibm-* catalog IDs and existing nodeType semantics. Bridge 0.8.3 advertises ibm-flowcharting-v1. Discover GET /flowchart/symbols with Read only to read all 43 labels, semantic nodeType defaults, category:symbol|outline|arrowhead|legacy, revisions, construction:cutout|composite|drawn, physicalCutout and shared outline/detail geometry. The revised IBM GX20-8020-1/-2 has 26 physical cutouts including four arrowheads; the catalog has 32 completed symbols, two raw apertures and four arrowheads. Five legacy entries retain the original Input/Output, Predefined Process, Program Modification, Clerical Operation and Perforated Tape meanings. revisions lists GX20-8020|GX20-8020-1|GX20-8020-2 outline membership; historical names/functions may differ for shared outlines; physicalCutout flags only the modern 26. GET /flowchart/stencils returns {revision,label,physicalCutoutSymbolIds,symbolLabels?} records for exact original 25 and revised 26 memberships; symbolLabels maps shared catalog IDs to their historical names. GET /templates and /templates/ibm-flowcharting return the complete editable example. POST /diagrams with {name,template:ibm-flowcharting,type?:flowchart} creates it with write access and rejects mode. Set flowchartSymbol when creating nodes, children or bulk entries, or through versioned node PATCH. Omitted partial fields preserve appearance; flowchartSymbol:null clears it only on PATCH or an existing bulk upsert. Complete/new records require omission or a catalog ID; null, empty and unknown IDs return 422 without partial writes. Appearance survives graph replacement, copy, native JSON, templates, backups and history without a schema migration. The catalog does not add simulation semantics; IBM Parallel Mode is a diagram symbol and Process Simulator fork/join remains separately configured."
